message: If you use this result, please cite the tagged release.
title: "The four possible weights in a two-field prime-race inverse"
abstract: "On two prime bands in the 547/727 and 571/599 races, the quartic for the weight at the integer start 13,471 has four real roots near the balanced target. Exactly one gives an admissible representation. The generic Galois group is S4, and the curves of unordered pairs and complementary partitions are linked by a degree-two isogeny. Every target in the full closed box admits three heights and weights in one real extension of degree at most four over the field generated by its coordinates, the real algebraic numbers and the prime logarithms in the construction. The sixteen corners have explicit certificates. These results use finite prime counts. Recurrence at arbitrarily late starts uses the critical-line hypothesis for the nontrivial zeros of the sixteen primitive odd Dirichlet L-functions, supplied by Alpöge’s announced Dirichlet GRH theorem."
